; The guards: the build gives an error if weft, weft.sim, weft.flow or
; weft-tls links unix (design section 2.3). The windtrap suites link unix, so
; each guard is a separate executable with no test library. weft-tls is
; optional (FreeBSD and Windows in CI have no tls), thus it has a guard of its
; own, and the guard of weft builds also where tls is absent.

(test
 (name nounix)
 (modules nounix)
 (libraries weft weft.sim weft.flow)
 (forbidden_libraries unix))

(test
 (name nounix_tls)
 (package weft-tls)
 (modules nounix_tls)
 (build_if %{lib-available:weft-tls})
 (libraries weft-tls)
 (forbidden_libraries unix))
